        "id": 1010013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-17T15:38:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e From the commit message \u0027However, those retries cause an illegal state exception[1]\n\u003e when inserting new changes is retried\u0027\n\u003e \n\u003e I was referring to this part of the message. My understanding was the any retry on change creation would cause this exception, thus suggestion to not retry in this case.\n\nThanks for clarifying. I think the original retries still make sense when it\u0027s a new PS on an existing change, so making those retries conditional likely makes sense. If that is impacting you, that probably should be done as a fix to the original change before even considering this change then. @Kaushik, does that make sense to you?\n\n\u003e In our setup, lock failures are also a common case, but they are normally caused by the stale replication, since AFAIK only the ref in local storage replica is updated synchronously.\n\nACK.",
      "parentUuid": "45ba9288_a43e89ac",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 32
      },
